    "# Python workout\n",
    "\n",
    "Nine exercises, easiest first. For each one:\n",
    "1. Read the docstring in the exercise cell.\n",
    "2. Replace `raise NotImplementedError` with your own code and run the cell.\n",
    "3. Run the check cell below it. If it prints \"passed\", move on.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the setup cell first. Use **Restart & Run All** if things act strangely.\n",
    ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import math, re, time\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "from functools import wraps\n",
    "import contextlib\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# tiny helpers so the checks need no extra packages\n",
    "class approx:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, v, rel=1e-6, abs=1e-12): self.v, self.rel, self.abs = v, rel, abs\n",
    "    def __eq__(self, o): return math.isclose(o, self.v, rel_tol=self.rel, abs_tol=self.abs)\n",
    "\n",
    "@contextlib.contextmanager\n",
    "def raises(exc):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        yield\n",
    "    except exc:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    raise AssertionError(f\"expected {exc.__name__} but nothing was raised\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Cleaning messy numbers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def clean_numbers(values):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Turn a list of messy values into floats, skipping anything invalid.\n",
    "\n",
    "    - Strings may contain thousands separators: \"1,200\" -> 1200.0\n",
    "    - Surrounding whitespace is allowed: \" 3.5 \" -> 3.5\n",
    "    - None, \"\", \"abc\" are skipped\n",
    "    - Ints and floats pass through as floats\n",
    "\n",
    "    >>> clean_numbers([\"1,200\", \" 3.5 \", None, \"abc\", 7])\n",
    "    [1200.0, 3.5, 7.0]\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    raise NotImplementedError"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def check_1():\n",
    "    assert clean_numbers([\"1,200\", \" 3.5 \", None, \"abc\", 7]) == [1200.0, 3.5, 7.0]\n",
    "    assert clean_numbers([]) == []\n",
    "    assert clean_numbers([\"\", \"  \", None]) == []\n",
    "    assert clean_numbers([2.5, \"-4\", \"1,000,000\"]) == [2.5, -4.0, 1_000_000.0]\n",
    "    print(\"Exercise 1 passed\")\n",
    "check_1()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
